From 7285036d5abc8686bbf3eeab4ab9729e7bab7012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:10:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENTAL spike: overlapped prompt read in pipelined batch
 mode (measurement only)

STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_SPIKE=1: in pipelined batch mode the prompt read runs on a worker thread
while the main thread keeps pumping the slot groups; adaptive swaps and the idle reset are held
meanwhile. Not production-safe (no PLE/graph-capture guards; see linux/upstream/DESIGN-overlap.md
for the full design). Measured on 4x RTX 3090: no throughput gain (decode drops to ~1/3 during a
read, the read stretches 10-20%), but median TTFT -70%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/program/generate.cpp | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/program/generate.cpp b/src/program/generate.cpp
index 1e92225..554b76b 100644
--- a/src/program/generate.cpp
+++ b/src/program/generate.cpp
